mapx=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured EPaxos package plus in-repository replica transport, master configuration, command execution and client admission; no other run inputs.',protocol_contexts=['Fixed participant rows, per-instance promises and value ballots, concurrent proposal owners'],external_interfaces=['Client PROPOSE TCP','Typed peer RPCs','Master registration and BeTheLeader RPC'],ownership=['Single protocol loop per replica; asynchronous transport and execution goroutines'],variants=['Default launcher: Thrifty true, Durable false, Dreply true, execution unless Noop'],source_ids=['S-init','S-config','S-base'],unknowns=['Crash-restart storage support and complete client retry policy remain unresolved.']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=surfaces,core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=path('Client admission batches commands into a new own-row instance. Local conflicts generate sequence/dependencies; PreAccept recipients qualify them against their history and return current context. Leader merges matching-ballot support. Initial-ballot equality and threshold permit fast commit; otherwise it sends Accept and counts a majority including self. Commit broadcasts full commands and attributes to alive peers; recipients reject lower ballots or already established decisions. Execution traverses committed dependencies, orders SCCs, updates the state machine and replies to retained clients. These are observed mechanisms, not proof of adequate quorum or agreement.',['B-propose','B-preaccept','B-form','B-accept','B-commit','B-execute'],['F-value','F-decision'],['S-phase1','S-pre-reply','S-accept','S-commit','S-exec']),context=path('Authority is per instance. Initial ballot is row owner ID. Recovery preserves proposals, resets bookkeeping and chooses a ballot congruent to the recovering replica, with higher-ballot adjustment conditional on IsLeader. Prepare raises a remote promise and returns retained value context. Initiator instead raises both promise and value ballot before self report. Matching Prepare replies fill a recovery quorum; maximum value ballot selects history, then status determines committed retention, Accept or restarted PreAccept. Master role assignment enables retry behavior but is not exclusive proposal ownership. Lower-ballot requests and mismatched replies are filtered; already queued messages remain independently dispatched.',['B-authority','B-select','B-recover-trigger','B-transport'],['F-value'],['S-recovery','S-exec-recovery','S-dispatch']),connection=path('The same local command/status/value-ballot record is both formed by proposal/accept/commit and consumed by later authority acquisition. Recovery is meant to carry eligible prior support into new formation: accepted selection re-enters Accept, committed selection stays committed, other selection restarts phase 1. Default execution detects stalled known instances and enqueues recovery. Local committed guards protect some old decisions, but report production/selection determines whether a new owner discovers another replica\'s decision. This producer-consumer distinction supplies the first question.',['B-propose','B-accept','B-commit','B-authority','B-select','B-recover-trigger'],['F-value','F-decision'],['S-phase1','S-accept','S-commit','S-recovery','S-exec-recovery']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Legal recovery history discriminating self-report promotion from prior committed support remains to construct.','Independent quorum, Accept status, optional persistence and SCAN leads remain sourced surfaces.'],rationale='Both core relationships and their connection are traced through read handlers, actual transport dispatch, recovery trigger, membership inputs and execution consumer. Local anomalies remain explicit; usable is navigation readiness, not correctness.'))
